LAST_SUCCESS=Phase 2b-ii steps 1-3 DONE + full warpkg builds (engine+ui+wac plug, 5.9M). (1) Safe deploy: build.sh --deploy backs up Signal /state before per-app install. (2) WIT: engine signal.wit gained audio import (deps/skiko-gfx/audio.wit) + call API in chat (place/accept/hangup-call, call-status, call-peer, call-incoming/call-state-changed events); synced to ui deps/signal/chat.wit; UI Event match got a minimal arm. (3) engine/src/call.rs = CallMessage<->CallSignal map + CallEngine (SignalCall + std::net UdpSocket + audio WIT pump, mic->send_audio/recv_audio->stereo track). (4) engine.rs: Shared call fields + CallIntent + place/accept/hangup/status/peer fns + run-loop wiring (inbound CallMessage dispatch, adaptive 10ms/200ms tick, intent drive, tick pump, send via send_signals! macro, sync_call_state). lib.rs generate_all + Guest call methods. Engine builds wasm32-wasip2. INTERIM: SRTP HKDF identity bound to ACIs (not real identity keys) — Phase 3 must replace for real-Signal interop. COMPILE-VERIFIED ONLY.
NOTES=NEXT step 4 (device test, 804KPSL1724590): deploy via ./build.sh --deploy (SAFE, backs up /state). Trigger a call between two linked wart Signal accounts (no UI yet — drive via a temp hook or add minimal in-call UI). Watch for: duplex audio MMAP (-889 open_capture+create_track same device), NAT (LAN-only host candidate; may need TURN across networks), the 10ms tick under step-executor, ACI-identity DH match. Then step 5: in-call UI screen (accept/hangup buttons + ringing). warpkg built at build/war.signal.warpkg.
